==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|snīþaną||to cut|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{recons|sneit-||to cut|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|snijden||to cut, carve, intersect|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|en|-}} {{term|snithe||to cut|lang=en}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{term|snida||to carve, engrave|lang=sv}}, {{etyl|is|-}} {{term|sníða||to trim, tailor|lang=is}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃnaɪ̯dn̩/|/ˈʃnaɪ̯dən/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-schneiden.ogg|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=1|schneidet|schnitt|geschnitten|past subjunctive=schnitte}}

# {{transitive}} to [[cut]]; to [[carve]]; to [[slice]]
# {{transitive}} to [[pare]]; to [[clip]]; to [[mow]]; to [[prune]]; to [[trim]]
# {{transitive|driving|figuratively|lang=de}} to cut (someone) off; to cut in on (someone)
# {{transitive|film|lang=de}} to [[edit]]
# {{transitive|or|reflexive|lang=de}} to [[intersect]]
#: ''Die beiden Geraden '''schneiden''' sich.'' — “Both streets intersect.”
# {{reflexive|lang=de}} to [[cut]] (oneself)
# {{reflexive|colloquial|lang=de}} to [[delude]] (oneself); to become mistaken
# to [[avoid]] somebody (to cut someone)
<!-- Are there any intransitive senses? -->

